# Notice of Crime: Motor Vehicle Theft, Core Campus, MPC
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D

In compliance with the "Timely Warning"=A0provisions of the federal Jeanne =
Clery Campus Safety Act, Virginia Commonwealth University is providing noti=
ce of a recently reported crimethat may pose a serious or continuing threat=
 to campus safety. This notice is intended to aid in the prevention of simi=
lar crimes and to enable members of the university community to protect the=
mselves. VCU is dedicated to promoting a safe and secure environment for le=
arning, living, working or visiting.=20

Reported offense: Motor Vehicle Theft (Motorized Scooter)

Location:=A012 N Brunswick St (VCU Dance Center)

Date and time of incident:=A0October 7, 2026 at 12:25 p.m.

Brief description of how the crime took place:=A0On October 7, 2026 at 12:4=
2 p.m., VCU Police was notified of the theft of a motorized scooter from th=
e above location.=A0 The vehicle was secured to a bike rack with a pink cab=
le lock.=A0 The scooter was described as a black ?Fifth Wheel? brand vehicl=
e. The suspect cut the cable lock with bolt cutters and left the scene in a=
 black Toyota Prius southbound towards W Main St.=20

Suspect/s:=A0For a full description of the suspect/s visit=A0alert.vcu.edu =
(<https://massmail.vcu.edu/trk/click?ref=3Dz173r7sgll_0-3470e_0_0x23b504x0=
53780>).

Investigating agency:=A0VCU Police are leading the investigation.=20

Anyone with information pertaining to any crime or suspicious activity shou=
ld contact the VCU Police Department at (804) 828-1234. For incidents occur=
ring off-campus in the city of Richmond, please call 911 for emergencies.

Anyone can submit tips, screenshots, photos and videos directly to VCU Poli=
ce via the VCU LiveSafe app, which is monitored 24/7. For more information,=
 visit police.vcu.edu/stay-safe/livesafe (<https://massmail.vcu.edu/trk/cli=
ck?ref=3Dz173r7sgll_0-3470e_0_0x251da5x053780>). Tips can als=
o be submitt=
ed to Metro Richmond Crime Stoppers at (804) 780-1000 or on the P3 Tips mob=
ile app; for more information, visit rvacrimestoppers.org/ (<https://massma=
il.vcu.edu/trk/click?ref=3Dz173r7sgll_0-3470e_0_0x251da6x0=
53780>).

VCU Police would like to remind the VCU and VCU Health community to keep pe=
rsonal safety in mind, be prepared and take responsibility for your own saf=
ety and for the safety of others. A few key reminders:

Motor Vehicle Theft (Cars, trucks, e-scooters, e-bikes):

 * Never leave your vehicle unattended, unlocked, running and/or with the k=
eys inside.
 * Always lock your car doors and windows.
 * Lock a motorcycle, scooter or e-bike to a stationary object that is immo=
vable, such as the end of a bike rack. Use a U-lock or a thick chain. Lock =
the forks or disc brakes.
 * Keep valuables in the trunk of your vehicle or take them with you.
 * Do not keep a spare key in your vehicle. This includes in your vehicle's=
 gas compartment.
 * If you see someone acting suspiciously near vehicles or bike racks, cont=
act VCU Police.

Transportation

VCU Parking and Transportation offers a variety of options to help communit=
y members travel between both campuses -- day and night. For more informati=
on, visit parking.vcu.edu/transportation/: <https://massmail.vcu.edu/trk/cl=
ick?ref=3Dz173r7sgll_0-3470e_0_0x251d4dx053780>.

